  "query_preview": "..\nToday and tonight: A fairly large upper low over the California \ncoast will keep an induced ridge to its east, allowing NE MT to \nexperience dry conditions and warmer than normal temps through \nearly Friday morning.\n\nFriday night into Saturday: But the upper low will begin to merge\nwith a western Canada trough tomorrow. This will pull up Pacific \nmoisture through the Desert SW while a surface low developing over\nsouthern MT and pulls NE tracking showers across the western CWA \nthrough Saturday morning. This will also allow NW winds to \nincrease late tomorrow behind a cold front. The showers are \nexpected to exit the CWA Saturday with significantly cooler high \ntemps Saturday onward.\n\nRough conditions on Fort Peck Lake can be expected beginning\nFriday afternoon through Saturday afternoon. A Lake wind advisory\nhas been issued for these times. \n\nRainfall amounts looked to be greatest over central Montana and\nthe models have shifted the deterministic rain amounts west with\nthis run. Areas east of a Culbertson to Miles City line are not\nexpecting any QPF.\n\nSaturday onward: Temps look to remain below to near normal as an \nupper ridge early next week doesn't nudge east of the Pac NW.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nNO changes to NBM.\n\nHigh confidence on winds and temperatures this weekend, and\nmoderate confidence on rain amounts.\n\nLow confidence Monday onward where ensembles bring zonal flow to\nthe area.",
